    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "THE PROBLEM",
      "t_start": 27.5,
      "estimated_duration_s": 9.5,
      "narration_text": "Photodynamic therapy mechanism: the drug reaches the tumor and sits inert. A fiber-optic then delivers light. The light activates the drug. Without light activation, nothing happens — the drug is pharmacologically silent.",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "am_onyx",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "form": "mechanism-pair",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "FormBCard",
          "provenance": "proven-core/FormBCard",
          "version": "1",
          "props": {
            "title": "PDT: drug + light = kill",
            "items": [
              {
                "label": "Drug",
                "sub": "sits inert",
                "icon": "BOX",
                "cueFrame": 20
              },
              {
                "label": "Light",
                "sub": "activates it",
                "icon": "BOX",
                "cueFrame": 80
              }
            ],
            "dark": false
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[CARD] drug + light -> activated killing",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.01,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T14:08:09"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "THE PROBLEM",
      "t_start": 37.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 9.0,
      "narration_text": "The delivery problem is therefore a light problem. Can the light physically reach the tumor? That depends entirely on tissue optics — how far light travels through flesh before it is attenuated to zero.",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "am_onyx",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "form": "reframe-card",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "FormACard",
          "provenance": "proven-core/FormACard",
          "version": "1",
          "props": {
            "lines": [
              "A delivery problem…",
              "…is a light problem.",
              "How far does light reach?"
            ],
            "dark": false
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[CARD] reframe: delivery → light",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.18,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T14:08:09"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "THE MECHANISM",
      "t_start": 46.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.0,
      "narration_text": "Red light at 630 nanometers — the wavelength used in photodynamic therapy — attenuates to near-zero within a few millimeters of tissue. Tissue scatters it and absorbs it. Intensity collapses exponentially with depth.",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "am_onyx",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "form": "attenuation-card",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "FormACard",
          "provenance": "proven-core/FormACard",
          "version": "1",
          "props": {
            "lines": [
              "630 nm red light in tissue",
              "  2 mm — 70% surface intensity",
              "  5 mm — 35%",
              "10 mm — 8%",
              "15 mm — under 2%"
            ],
            "dark": false
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "new_visual_element": "[CHART] light intensity decays exponentially with depth",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.61,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-30T14:08:09"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "THE MECHANISM",
      "t_start": 57.0,
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.0,
      "narration_text": "Red and near-infrared light were chosen specifically because they penetrate furthest. This is the best optical window tissue provides. Even so, effective treatment depth is measured in millimeters — at most one centimeter under ideal conditions.",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "am_onyx",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
